{"id": "EUVD-2026-102293", "enisaUuid": "e1549dcc-cdff-3878-bff6-5ce9d3f0a982", "description": "libmikmod through 3.3.15 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the IMF_Load() loader that allows attackers to read beyond allocated memory by supplying a crafted IMF module. Attackers can enable the linear-period header flag and map notes to out-of-range samples, causing noteindex indexing far past the heap allocation and crashing applications that load the file.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:31:56", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libmikmod-mtm-imf-loader-oob-read", "https://github.com/sezero/mikmod/blob/6e658155f7e6b394a288dac796ba572634553fad/libmikmod/loaders/load_imf.c#L702-L712", "https://github.com/sezero/mikmod", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libmikmod-through-3.3.15-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-imf-load"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111166", "GHSA-pcxh-23x2-w962"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "74136705-b817-349b-b2fb-db22d8982f7a", "product": {"name": "libmikmod", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.3.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9530f5a8-aba9-3687-ab43-21fba0cbf3b2", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}], "isExploited": false}